From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Leung <untilscour@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 09:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: publish wcid before MCU add commands

mt7915 interface setup enables the BSS and STA in firmware before
publishing dev->mt76.wcid[idx]. Firmware can generate TX status or TX
free events as soon as it processes those commands, leaving the event
handlers without a published WCID and potentially causing memory
corruption.

Publish the WCID before telling firmware that the interface is live.
Apply the ordering in mt7915_init_vif(), where the MediaTek testmode
patches moved the common interface setup, so normal and beamforming
test interfaces both use the safe lifetime order.

Closes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/24594
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260821-mt7915-wcid-publish-order-v2-1-acf0b7f32cbd@protonmail.com
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24810
Signed-off-by: Ryan Leung <untilscour@protonmail.com>
---
 mt7915/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -322,9 +322,9 @@ int mt7915_init_vif(struct mt7915_phy *p
 	mt7915_init_bitrate_mask(vif);
 	memset(&mvif->cap, -1, sizeof(mvif->cap));
 
+	rcu_assign_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[idx], &mvif->sta.wcid);
 	mt7915_mcu_add_bss_info(phy, vif, true);
 	mt7915_mcu_add_sta(dev, vif, NULL, CONN_STATE_PORT_SECURE, true);
-	rcu_assign_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[idx], &mvif->sta.wcid);
 
 	if (!is_mt7915(&dev->mt76))
 		mt7915_mcu_set_vow_band(dev, mvif);
